A quick note on this because it's maybe interesting:

These 21 apes are not truly bricked forever. They can be swapped for other apes using the same mechanism run this morning.

But all of the listings are cleared - ApeSTR effectively thinks it owns 0 apes - so nothing can be purchased.

So to you purists saying this is a deflationary event - it kind of is?

There are net-new 21 apes that can never be purchased, but which 21 those are can change from day to day.

@DGMD22 @mikematvei Yeah, correctly. And not really anything new either, just that this time it had unfortunate side effects.

When apecoin dropped people did something similar with NFTX apes

